@startuml activity-risk
title FinRisk - Risk score calculation (swimlanes, with formulas)

skinparam shadowing false
skinparam DefaultFontName Arial
skinparam ActivityBackgroundColor #f6f9fc
skinparam ActivityBorderColor #3b6ea5
skinparam ActivityDiamondBackgroundColor #f6f9fc
skinparam ActivityDiamondBorderColor #3b6ea5
skinparam PartitionBorderColor #3b6ea5
skinparam PartitionBackgroundColor #f0f4fa
skinparam NoteBackgroundColor #fff9d6
skinparam NoteBorderColor #c2b96a
skinparam ArrowColor #3b6ea5
skinparam LegendBackgroundColor #fff9d6
skinparam LegendBorderColor #c2b96a

|User|
start
:GET /api/v1/accounts/{id}/risk-score;

|RiskController|
:Receive HTTP request;

|RiskService|
:Load account holdings;
note right
  Each holding has
  assetId, symbol,
  quantity, currentValue V_j
end note

:Compute portfolio total value
**V = sum_j V_j**;

if (V <= 0?) then (yes)
  :Return RiskScoreResponse
  score = 0.0,  level = LOW,
  breakdown = empty list;
  |User|
  :Receive RiskScore response;
  stop
else (no)
endif

|RiskService|
:Compute holding weights
**w_j = V_j / V**;
note right
  Weights sum to 1.0.
  Larger holdings dominate
  the final portfolio number.
end note

repeat :For each holding j;

  |DAOs and SQL Server|
  :Query asset_price_history
  (latest 30 rows, newest-first);

  |RiskService|
  :Reverse to chronological order
  p_0, p_1, ..., p_N
  (oldest -> newest);

  if (enough samples ? N+1 >= minSamples = 5) then (yes)

    |VolatilityRiskStrategy|
    :**Step 1 - log returns**
    r_i = ln( p_i / p_(i-1) )
    for i = 1..N;
    note right
      Log returns make
      gains and losses
      symmetric and additive.
    end note

    :**Step 2 - mean of returns**
    mu = (1/N) * sum_i r_i;

    :**Step 3 - sample variance**
    var = ( 1 / (N-1) ) * sum_i (r_i - mu)^2;
    note right
      Bessel correction
      (N-1, not N) - unbiased
      estimate from a sample.
    end note

    :**Step 4 - daily volatility**
    sigma_j = sqrt(var);

    :**Step 5 - map sigma to RiskLevel**
    sigma < 0.01      -> LOW
    sigma < 0.03      -> MEDIUM
    sigma < 0.06      -> HIGH
    sigma >= 0.06     -> VERY_HIGH;

  else (too few samples)
    |VolatilityRiskStrategy|
    :Use intrinsic asset risk
    level_j = asset.calculateRiskLevel()
    (Stock=HIGH, ETF=MEDIUM,
     Bond=LOW, Crypto=VERY_HIGH);

    :**Fallback sigma**
    sigma_j = {
      LOW:0.005, MEDIUM:0.02,
      HIGH:0.045, VERY_HIGH:0.08
    }[ level_j ];
  endif

  |RiskService|
  :Append breakdown item
  (assetId, symbol, level_j,
   weight w_j, sigma_j, samples);

repeat while (more holdings?) is (yes)
->no;

:**Aggregate portfolio sigma**
sigma_p = sum_j ( w_j * sigma_j );
note right
  Value-weighted average:
  each asset contributes in
  proportion to its share
  of portfolio value.
end note

:**Map portfolio sigma to RiskLevel**
portfolio_level = levelForSigma(sigma_p);

:**Scale to score in [0, 100]**
score = min( 100.0, (sigma_p / 0.12) * 100.0 );
note right
  0.12 daily sigma ~ very risky;
  anything above is clipped to 100.
end note

|RiskController|
:Build RiskScoreResponse
(accountId, score, portfolio_level,
 breakdown[]);

|User|
:Receive RiskScore response;
stop

legend bottom
  **What this shows.**
  How FinRisk turns raw daily prices into a single risk number per portfolio.
  For each holding we pull the last 30 closing prices, convert them to
  **log returns** r_i = ln(p_i / p_(i-1)), compute the **sample standard
  deviation** sigma (Bessel-corrected, N-1 in the denominator), and that
  sigma is the asset's volatility. When we don't have enough history we
  fall back to a fixed sigma based on the asset's intrinsic risk level.
  We then take a **value-weighted average** sigma_p = sum (w_j * sigma_j),
  classify it with the LOW/MEDIUM/HIGH/VERY_HIGH thresholds, and scale it
  to a 0-100 score using 0.12 daily sigma as the "100" anchor.
endlegend

@enduml
